{"name":"Golden Pastel","hex":"#f4d9b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"pastel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several subdued tints of colors, usually associated with pink, peach, yellow, green, blue, and lavender.","A drawing made with any of those colors."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional dish in various Latin American countries and in Indonesia, resembling a tamale, pasty, or calzone.","A Filipino stew made with vegetables, sausages, and chicken or other meat in a creamy sauce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pastel","blocks":[{"text":"A pastel is an art medium that consists of powdered pigment and a binder. It can exist in a variety of forms, including a stick, a square, a pebble, and a pan of color, among other forms. The pigments used in pastels are similar to those used to produce some other colored visual arts media, such as oil paints; the binder is of a neutral hue and low saturation. The color effect of pastels is closer to the natural dry pigments than that of any other process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg/330px-William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel","wikidata":"Q189085"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"},{"title":"Pastel (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Pastels or pastel colors belong to a pale family of colors, which, when described in the HSV color space, have high value and low or medium saturation. They are named after the artistic medium made from pigment and solid binding agents, similar to crayons. Pastel sticks historically had lower saturation than paints of the same pigment, hence the name of this color family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Commercial_pastels.JPG/330px-Commercial_pastels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel_(color)","wikidata":"Q2513175"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/500px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/1280px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/500px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maurice Quentin de La Tour, a bravura pastel portrait of Louis XV, 1748","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouis15-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odilon Redon, Baronne de Domecy, c. 1900, pastel and graphite on light brown laid paper, J. Paul Getty Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOdilon_Redon_(French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg/500px-Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg/1280px-Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg/500px-Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Edgar Degas, La Danseuse Rose, Pastel on canvas, 93 × 73 cm - 36 5/8 × 28 3/4 in. (Ex-collection of Sita Devi, Maharani of Baroda)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Frottage_02.jpg/500px-Frottage_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Frottage_02.jpg/1280px-Frottage_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte